msub space=\"4\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D6FC TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>⋯</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n<p>Each sum of squares equals the sum of squares <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"eq-ss-hypothesis\">@eq-ss-hypothesis</span> of the hypothesis\nit addresses, in the cell-means model.</p>","file":"ch09-sums-of-squares/03-sequential-partial.html"}